  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nBoundary layer winds will likely weaken on a daily basis amid\nmostly cloud free conditions during the nights. While valleys\nwill likely decouple, valley fog will have the potential to \nform on a daily basis with light to calm wind, the lack of \nclouds and a weaker boundary layer wind along with radiational \ncooling will all help temperatures fall to the dewpoints and \npromote fog on a daily basis. Some of the fog could become \ndense at certain locations, however most of the fog should be \nconfined to the river valleys. Fog will dissipate by mid morning\neach day. Minor impacts from fog will likely take place if \ndriving in the hollers and deep valleys who receive cold air \ndrainage. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure with strong upper level ridging will prevail in \nthe short term providing pleasant and quiet weather. A \ndisturbance is forecast to slide to our south for late tonight \nand through Saturday morning. This will provide some slight \nchances or rain to the extreme southern portions of the county \nwarning area. \n\nAnother disturbance will have the potential to bring showers \nand/or thunderstorms to the area from Sunday evening through \nMonday afternoon. This will be confined to the southern portions\nof the county warning area once again but will likely make its \nway up into the coal fields and close to the Tri-state and \nCharleston Metro area. Therefore, we cannot rule out a few \nstorms during peak heating hours. This will include our \nsouthwestern VA counties as well. \n\nAnother larger disturbance, a cut-off low, coming in from the\nnorth will setup just east of the area by midweek. This feature\ncould potentially cause some rain and possible thunderstorm \nactivity to get into the northeast sector of the area on \nWednesday. High pressure will then prevent the feature from \ntraversing into the area and should keep the area settled the \nrest of the work week. \n\nImpacts to the rest of the area will remain very quiet amid \nhigh pressure and the lack of any rainfall chances. Temperatures\nwill remain fairly seasonable and pleasant for the short and \nlong term forecast periods.",
